{title: Hard Times Come Again No More}
{artist: Stephen Foster, 1854}
{key: D}
{tempo: 70}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: folk, americana}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
Let us [D]pause in life's [G]pleasures and [D]count its many tears
While we [D]all sup [A]sorrow with the poor
There's a [D]song that will [G]linger for[D]ever in our ears
Oh! [D]Hard times [A]come again no [D]more

{start_of_chorus}
'Tis the [D]song, the [G]sigh of the [D]weary
Hard times, hard times, [A]come again no more
Many [D]days you have [G]lingered a[D]round my cabin door
Oh! [D]Hard times [A]come again no [D]more
